From: iiAhmedYT <61851106+iiAhmedYT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:02:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Guard chunk unload against corrupted block entity maps

A chunk's block entity map can be corrupted by an off-thread writer, for
example a plugin touching chunk data from a non-tick thread. Iterating it
during ServerLevel#unload then throws NullPointerException,
ConcurrentModificationException or ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException, which
aborts the world tick and crashes the server with 'Exception ticking world'.

Catch those three exception types around the block entity loop, log the
chunk position, dimension and exception once, and continue the unload as
normal. Throwable is deliberately not caught so real errors still surface.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
index 8ab5d05bd88acfa21bc0237e3556b441c5425dea..05a5832bf29a3ac70e85d85340dbd92a78f922a8 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -1985,17 +1985,24 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements WorldGenLevel, ServerEntityGet
 
     public void unload(final LevelChunk levelChunk) {
         // Spigot start
-        for (net.minecraft.world.level.block.entity.BlockEntity blockEntity : levelChunk.getBlockEntities().values()) {
-            if (blockEntity instanceof net.minecraft.world.Container) {
-                // Paper start - this area looks like it can load chunks, change the behavior
-                // chests for example can apply physics to the world
-                // so instead we just change the active container and call the event
-                for (org.bukkit.entity.HumanEntity human : Lists.newArrayList(((net.minecraft.world.Container) blockEntity).getViewers())) {
-                    ((org.bukkit.craftbukkit.entity.CraftHumanEntity) human).getHandle().closeUnloadedInventory(org.bukkit.event.inventory.InventoryCloseEvent.Reason.UNLOADED); // Paper - Inventory close reason
+        // Leaf start - Guard against corrupted block entity maps during chunk unload
+        try {
+            for (net.minecraft.world.level.block.entity.BlockEntity blockEntity : levelChunk.getBlockEntities().values()) {
+                if (blockEntity instanceof net.minecraft.world.Container) {
+                    // Paper start - this area looks like it can load chunks, change the behavior
+                    // chests for example can apply physics to the world
+                    // so instead we just change the active container and call the event
+                    for (org.bukkit.entity.HumanEntity human : Lists.newArrayList(((net.minecraft.world.Container) blockEntity).getViewers())) {
+                        ((org.bukkit.craftbukkit.entity.CraftHumanEntity) human).getHandle().closeUnloadedInventory(org.bukkit.event.inventory.InventoryCloseEvent.Reason.UNLOADED); // Paper - Inventory close reason
+                    }
+                    // Paper end - this area looks like it can load chunks, change the behavior
                 }
-                // Paper end - this area looks like it can load chunks, change the behavior
             }
+        } catch (NullPointerException | java.util.ConcurrentModificationException | ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException ex) {
+            // The block entity map of a chunk can be corrupted by off-thread writes. Never let that abort the unload.
+            LOGGER.error("Failed to process block entities of chunk {} in dimension {} while unloading, continuing unload", levelChunk.getPos(), this.dimension().identifier(), ex);
         }
+        // Leaf end - Guard against corrupted block entity maps during chunk unload
         // Spigot end
         levelChunk.clearAllBlockEntities();
         levelChunk.unregisterTickContainerFromLevel(this);
